From bb3b75f669db6f4dc04e79e2b1cf74de78496a8a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
Date: Sat, 28 Nov 2026 15:02:44 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 4/8] rescue: report the system state and the boot log
 (task-90)

Two read-only v3 endpoints plus the matching /status keys:

- GET /sysinfo returns the frozen key list from the v3 contract:
  version and build strings, board/SoC/CPU, DRAM size, the SPI-NAND
  geometry and ID, the CP15 registers and the clock registers the rescue
  can see. The CP15 reads reuse the e2631soc helpers, now exported through
  e2631soc.h, so e2631soc and /sysinfo cannot disagree about the core.
- GET /log returns the boot-log snapshot taken once at the e2631rescue
  entry from the console record ring, with X-E2631-Log-Bytes/Overflow
  headers and the download disposition for ?download=1. Rescue traffic
  after the snapshot does not change it.
- /status gains log_bytes and log_overflow.

Neither endpoint writes flash or the environment.

Signed-off-by: QC3284 <2078725082@qq.com>
---
